{"object":"Jurisdiction and product context. A generic standards list does not establish that an exact model and lot has a valid certification in the owner's jurisdiction.","predicate":"vary_by","source_url":"http://localhost:8090/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic/Electrical_safety_standards","subject":"electronic product safety standards","text":"Electronic product makers must account for applicable safety standards, and the frozen standards evidence lists different jurisdictional systems. This establishes the need to bind a certification to the exact model and jurisdiction, not that any captured listing has done so.","title":"prop_safety_standards_boundary"}